    "summary_insights": [
      "Revenue declined by 12.7% year-on-year, falling from £2.28m to £1.99m, primarily driven by a reduction in renovation and new build activity.",
      "Gross margin compressed from 35.0% to 31.5%, indicating rising direct costs relative to turnover, particularly in direct labour which rose despite falling sales.",
      "Operating profit saw a significant contraction of 52.1%, dropping from £463k to £222k due to the combined impact of lower revenue and higher overheads.",
      "Administrative expenses increased by 21.0%, largely influenced by a 51.2% rise in depreciation charges and increased director pension contributions.",
      "Net profit margin weakened considerably from 16.3% to 9.6%, reflecting reduced operational efficiency and higher fixed costs.",
      "The company remains debt-free with no interest payable, though the sharp decline in profitability suggests a need for tighter cost control.",
      "Dividend payments were reduced from £198k to £149k, aligning with the lower net profit for the year.",
      "Staff costs and directors' remuneration increased despite the top-line decline, representing a significant headwind to net earnings."
    ]
  },
